.TH qsh-trust-deny 1  "deny 0.5.8" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-trust\-deny \- Withdraw actions granted with `qsh trust allow` (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0051 결정 12). A running serve notices within a poll tick and closes the pin\*(Aqs established connections that lost an action (ADR\-0031). Does not touch the role: use `qsh trust set\-role` for it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh trust deny\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fINAME\fR> <\fIACTION\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Withdraw actions granted with `qsh trust allow` (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0051 결정 12). A running serve notices within a poll tick and closes the pin\*(Aqs established connections that lost an action (ADR\-0031). Does not touch the role: use `qsh trust set\-role` for it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR
Never run ssh on this command\*(Aqs behalf: no automatic bootstrap of an unknown name, and no restarting of a pinned host\*(Aqs serve over ssh when the connection fails (`docs/CLI.md` §7). `qsh pair ssh` is not affected; it is ssh by definition
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
The pinned peer\*(Aqs name
.TP
<\fIACTION\fR>
Actions to withdraw
.SH VERSION
v0.5.8
